/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 0 -16 Td (Straight duct friction head loss is fundamentally governed by the Darcy-Weisbach equation:) Tj
/F5 10 Tf 0.1 0.2 0.4 rg 20 -17 Td (Delta_Pf = f * [ L / Dh ] * Pv  [in. w.g.]) Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg -20 -16 Td (where friction factor f is given by the implicit Colebrook-White equation for turbulent flow in) Tj
0 -13 Td (galvanized steel ducts with absolute surface roughness epsilon = 0.0003 ft \(0.09 mm\):) Tj
/F5 9.5 Tf 0.1 0.2 0.4 rg 20 -17 Td (1 / sqrt[f] = -2 * log10[ (epsilon / 3.7*Dh) + (2.51 / Re*sqrt[f]) ]) Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg -20 -17 Td (Across commercial HVAC sizing ranges \(600 to 3000 FPM, 4 to 60 in. duct\), Tool-6 evaluates the) Tj
0 -13 Td (standard ASHRAE/SMACNA power-law relationship, which correlates within +/-1.2% of Colebrook:) Tj
/F5 10.5 Tf 0.1 0.2 0.4 rg 20 -20 Td (DFL = [ 0.10913 * Q^1.90 ] / [ De^5.02 ]  [in. w.g. / 100 ft]) Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg -20 -18 Td (where Q = airflow rate in CFM, and De = Huebscher circular equivalent diameter in inches.) Tj
0 -14 Td (For a straight duct section of physical length L \(feet\), the total static pressure drop is:) Tj
/F5 10 Tf 0.1 0.2 0.4 rg 20 -18 Td (Delta_P_straight = [ L / 100 ] * DFL  [in. w.g.]) Tj
