/F1 13 Tf 0.06 0.15 0.32 rg 54 720 Td (5. Fitting Loss Formulation & The Unified Bridge Constant \(K_ref\)) Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 0 -16 Td (HVAC design historically employs two distinct methods for calculating fitting dynamic losses:) Tj
0 -13 Td (1. The SMACNA / ASHRAE Loss Coefficient \(Co\) Method:   Delta_P = Co * Pv) Tj
0 -13 Td (2. The Loren Cook Equivalent Length \(Leq\) Method:        Delta_P = Leq * 0.001 * [V / 1350]^2) Tj
0 -14 Td (Loren Cook defines Leq at catalog reference conditions: V_ref = 1350 FPM and DFL_ref = 0.10 in./100'.) Tj

/F1 11 Tf 0.06 0.15 0.32 rg 0 -22 Td (Mathematical Unification Proof:) Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 0 -15 Td (Velocity pressure at V_ref = 1350 FPM is:   Pv_ref = [1350 / 4005]^2 = 0.11362206 in. w.g.) Tj
0 -13 Td (Equating SMACNA static loss to equivalent length friction loss at the catalog reference point:) Tj
/F5 9.5 Tf 0.1 0.2 0.4 rg 20 -16 Td (Co * Pv_ref = [Leq / 100] * DFL_ref) Tj
0 -13 Td (Co * 0.11362206 = [Leq / 100] * 0.10 = Leq * 0.001) Tj
0 -13 Td (Co / Leq = 0.001 / 0.11362206 = 1 / 113.62706) Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg -20 -15 Td (We define the Unified Cook-SMACNA Reference Constant \(K_ref\):) Tj
/F5 10.5 Tf 0.06 0.15 0.32 rg 20 -18 Td (K_ref = 100 * [ (1350 / 4005)^2 ] / 0.10 = 113.62706 ft) Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg -20 -16 Td (Unified Loss Formulation implemented in Tool-6:) Tj
/F5 10.5 Tf 0.1 0.2 0.4 rg 20 -18 Td (Co = Leq / 113.627) Tj
0 -14 Td (Delta_P_fitting = Co * Pv = [ Leq / 113.627 ] * [ V / 4005 ]^2  [in. w.g.]) Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg -20 -16 Td (Mathematical Identity Verification:) Tj
0 -13 Td ([Leq / 113.627] * [V / 4005]^2  =  Leq * 0.001 * [V / 1350]^2   [Q.E.D.]) Tj
0 -13 Td (This identity guarantees that fitting loss scales precisely with V^2 at all velocities.) Tj

/F1 11 Tf 0.06 0.15 0.32 rg 0 -22 Td (6. Continuous Interpolation Engine Overview) Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 0 -14 Td (Tool-6 replaces discrete nearest-neighbor snapping with continuous mathematical surface models:) Tj
0 -13 Td (- 1D Piecewise Linear: y\(x\) = y0 + [\(x - x0\) / \(x1 - x0\)] * \(y1 - y0\) across ordered catalog breakpoints.) Tj
0 -13 Td (- 2D Bilinear Surface: y\(u, v\) = y_j\(v\) + [\(u - u_j\) / \(u_{j+1} - u_j\)] * [y_{j+1}\(v\) - y_j\(v\)] across velocity/flow matrices.) Tj
ET
endstream
